course: dictionary
lesson: 8601
title: Words with a place in them
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a person comes from. A Scotsman is a man from Scotland, and a Scotswoman is a woman from Scotland. Scots and Scottish people are words for everyone from Scotland, women and men together.
explain: Capital letters and the words around a name give you clues. «The Scotsman» is the name of a newspaper in Edinburgh, not a man. «The Flying Scotsman» is the name of a famous steam train. Ask yourself: is this a person, a paper, or a train?
explain: The example sentence «Changing what a word means so that you win is a trap called "no true Scotsman".» uses Scotsman as part of a name for a trick in an argument. The meaning of the word does not change, but the phrase does a different job. Always read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: A Scotsman is a man from Scotland.
fact: A Scotswoman is a woman from Scotland.
fact: «The Scotsman» is the name of a newspaper in Edinburgh.
fact: «The Flying Scotsman» was a famous steam train that ran between London and Edinburgh.
fact: «No true Scotsman» is the name of a trap in arguing: changing what a word means so that you win.
exercise: «A proud Scotsman stood up and sang.» What is a Scotsman? | *A man from Scotland | A newspaper in Edinburgh | A kind of Scottish dinner | A steam train
exercise: «The Flying Scotsman» was a famous steam train. Where did it run? | Only in the Lake District | *Between London and Edinburgh | Under the sea | Between Glasgow and Paris
exercise: Priya's gran is from Scotland and she is a woman. What do we call her? | A steam train | *A Scotswoman | A Scotsman | A newspaper
test: In «The Scotsman», what is the Scotsman? | A man from Scotland | A kind of tartan | A famous steam train | *A newspaper in Edinburgh
test: Which word covers all people from Scotland, women and men? | *Scots | Scotsmen | Scotswoman | Flying Scotsman
exam: In «The Flying Scotsman», what kind of thing is it? | A man from Scotland | A woman from Scotland | A newspaper | *A famous steam train
